# Store install.cmd bytes as CRLF. Do not mark it "text" or "eol=crlf":
# those attributes keep LF in the git blob, and the Windows install curls
# that blob from raw.githubusercontent.com. cmd.exe resets its 512-byte
# label scan only on CRLF, so an LF-only file can miss a real label
# (call :NeedTool) when the label straddles a chunk boundary.
install.cmd -text
